From: mastergray <mastergray@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] capture a deterministic native/browser parity checkpoint

Capture the hidden native render target after a fixed emulated-frame warmup
and exercise one digital input through the core port boundary.  The same code
runs in native and Emscripten builds so geometry, refresh, RGBA hash and input
transitions can be compared without wall-clock screenshot timing.

The minimal native OSD deliberately has no host font provider; return no OSD
font so the core falls back to its embedded UI font instead of dereferencing
the uninitialized modular-font pointer.

The selected legacy driver family also shares an audio device between
configurations with and without a sample-ROM region.  Treat the absent region
as an empty sample source instead of relying on a null dereference that happens
not to trap in WebAssembly linear memory.

--- a/src/osd/osdmini/osdmini.h
+++ b/src/osd/osdmini/osdmini.h
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@ public:
 	// general overridables
 	virtual void init(running_machine &machine);
 	virtual void update(bool skip_redraw);
+	virtual osd_font *font_alloc() { return NULL; }
 };
 
 
--- a/src/mame/audio/m72.c
+++ b/src/mame/audio/m72.c
@@ -72,8 +72,9 @@ void m72_audio_device::device_config_complete()
 
 void m72_audio_device::device_start()
 {
-	m_samples = machine().root_device().memregion("samples")->base();
-	m_samples_size = machine().root_device().memregion("samples")->bytes();
+	memory_region *samples = machine().root_device().memregion("samples");
+	m_samples = samples == NULL ? NULL : samples->base();
+	m_samples_size = samples == NULL ? 0 : samples->bytes();
 	m_space = &machine().device("soundcpu")->memory().space(AS_IO);
 	m_dac = machine().device<dac_device>("dac");
 

